Requirements and verification sync for small FPV drone

11/8/26
What I did: 
Created a google colab python script to grant OAuth to my gaccount. 
Defined a variable gc as a client that carries my creds, then ran the open function within the client. 
Defined variable raw as the "raw" tab in my "FPV Drone Requirements" spreadsheet. Called raw to display within the colab window.
I called a GET request to gsheets and returned my gsheet data formatted nicely via the pandas library in gspread.
What broke:
I purposefully didnt authorize the gcloud permissions in the OAuth, and the script broke due to incorrect permissions.
How I fixed it:
Re-ran the script and gave all permissions. Least privilege is a valid concern, but restricting necessary privileges can cause an auth to fail.
Service accounts can be used to manage permissions to company wide files. An auth is scoped to the entire service account, but the customer
only grants permission to the service account for the assetts they choose. Service account ccess can be revoked at any time, therefore revoking the APIs access to the files.
